html=sub(r'<p><!-- LEAD:BODY -->.*?</p>','<p><!-- LEAD:BODY --> Midday finds the foothills under a partly sunny sky, <b>high near 54 with temperatures easing to about 48 this afternoon</b>. The morning&#8217;s <b>traffic hazard in the snow just west of Ellis Rd on SR-88 has cleared off the CHP board</b> — it is no longer listed at the midday read. <b>Chain control still stands in the CHP log on SR-88</b>: the Stockton board (updated 12:31 PM) still carries its 5:46 AM chain-control entry at <b>SR-88 / Kirkwood Meadows Dr</b>, even though Caltrans&#8217; midday web report lists no chain-control segment — the desk carries the CHP log as governing, as it did Sunday evening. Caltrans adds a foothill note of its own: <b>one-way controlled traffic for tree work on SR-88 near the SR-124 junction</b>, 8:00 AM–5:00 PM today and tomorrow. <b>No National Weather Service alert is in effect</b> for the Fiddletown point; tonight is partly cloudy, low near 41. <b>SR-49 and SR-124 report no restrictions.</b> Of today&#8217;s three database listings, the <b>Sierra Oak Farms veggie stand</b> is selling at Fiddletown Rd and Mt. Whitney today and tomorrow, Ione&#8217;s Preschool Story Time has run, and the <b>Jackson City Council meets at City Hall at 6:30 PM</b>. The week&#8217;s wet stretch has lightened since morning: Tuesday turns partly sunny, high near 59, with rain only a chance Tuesday night, and Wednesday now reads mostly sunny — Thanksgiving Day stays mostly sunny, high near 61. <!-- /LEAD:BODY --></p>',html,flags=re.S,label="lead body")

